# SSH inventory fixture for the E2E suite.
#
# Both hosts are deliberately unreachable, in two different ways, so the suite
# stays hermetic: it never touches infrastructure, and every run fails the same
# way. Do not point these at anything real.

# A closed port on the loopback interface: the connection is refused
# immediately, so an execution against it reaches a terminal failure in
# milliseconds. This is the target for admission and failure-display tests.
# Groups: e2e
Host e2e-refused
  HostName 127.0.0.1
  Port 1
  User e2e

# A port the test opens itself with a TCP listener that accepts the connection
# and then says nothing, so the SSH handshake waits for a banner that never
# arrives and the run stays busy until its timeout. This is the target for
# tests that need work still running, such as cancelling the execution queued
# behind it. Nothing listens here unless a test is running.
#
# It is addressed as "localhost" while the refused host uses the literal
# 127.0.0.1, so node linking sees two hosts rather than merging them into one.
# Groups: e2e
Host e2e-stalled
  HostName localhost
  Port 45001
  User e2e
